1
00:00:00,010 --> 00:01:25,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

3
00:01:26,738 --> 00:01:30,220
Any minute now. You see,
you can't rush it, baby girl.

4
00:01:30,264 --> 00:01:33,267
The secret to fishing
is patience.

5
00:01:33,310 --> 00:01:35,791
It's been
five hours, Dad.

6
00:01:35,834 --> 00:01:38,185
How much more patience
do we need?

7
00:01:38,228 --> 00:01:41,188
Don't ask me.
Ask the fish.

8
00:01:42,406 --> 00:01:44,539
What's up, guys?
It's your boy, Dustin.

9
00:01:44,582 --> 00:01:46,497
I'm out on the boat,
and once again,

10
00:01:46,541 --> 00:01:49,065
my dad can't catch
any fish.

11
00:01:49,109 --> 00:01:50,980
Hey! I heard that.

12
00:01:51,023 --> 00:01:53,765
Don't worry, sweetheart,
I caught these this morning.

13
00:01:53,809 --> 00:01:55,637
At the grocery store.

14
00:01:55,680 --> 00:01:59,031
Mom, I'm live!
So embarrassing!

15
00:02:08,215 --> 00:02:10,652
Mr. Fluffy Butt, no!

16
00:02:10,695 --> 00:02:11,653
Bad kitty!

17
00:02:14,134 --> 00:02:15,483
Whoa.

18
00:02:15,526 --> 00:02:16,527
Uh... Dad?

19
00:02:16,571 --> 00:02:17,572
Dad!

20
00:02:17,615 --> 00:02:20,488
Shh! Quiet.
You'll scare the fishies.

21
00:02:20,531 --> 00:02:22,446
The boat's on fire!

22
00:02:32,108 --> 00:02:34,458
Down! Ready... set.

23
00:02:34,980 --> 00:02:35,851
Ruff!

24
00:02:37,069 --> 00:02:39,028
Skye! Skye, I'm open!

25
00:02:39,071 --> 00:02:40,421
Marshall, go long!

26
00:02:42,031 --> 00:02:44,512
I got it. I got it. I-- Whoa!

27
00:02:46,557 --> 00:02:48,777
Oof!

28
00:02:48,820 --> 00:02:50,779
Marshall!

29
00:02:50,822 --> 00:02:52,520
I'm okay!

30
00:02:52,563 --> 00:02:55,000
Pass is incomplete.
Flag on the play.

31
00:02:55,044 --> 00:02:56,654
Ten yards for clumsiness.

32
00:03:01,398 --> 00:03:03,226
<i>Mayday, mayday! S.O.S.!</i>

33
00:03:03,270 --> 00:03:05,663
<i>Our cat set our boat on fire!</i>

34
00:03:05,707 --> 00:03:07,143
This is the PAW Patrol.

35
00:03:07,187 --> 00:03:09,493
S.O.S. received.
We're on our way.

36
00:03:14,585 --> 00:03:17,153
Come on, pups.
Ryder needs us.

37
00:03:20,765 --> 00:03:24,421
That was my first touchdown!
It's still gonna count, right?

38
00:03:25,161 --> 00:03:26,423
Hey, wait up!

39
00:03:27,685 --> 00:03:28,730
<i>All right, pups.</i>

40
00:03:28,773 --> 00:03:30,340
<i>We've got</i>
<i>a five-alarm boat fire</i>

41
00:03:30,384 --> 00:03:32,037
<i>and there are people onboard.</i>

42
00:03:33,604 --> 00:03:36,607
<i>Zuma, you are go for launch.</i>

43
00:03:36,651 --> 00:03:38,087
Aye-aye, Ryder, sir!

44
00:03:49,054 --> 00:03:51,840
<i>Skye, let's get eyes</i>
<i>on that boat ASAP.</i>

45
00:03:51,883 --> 00:03:53,189
I'm on it.

46
00:03:56,497 --> 00:03:59,674
Marshall, Chase, Rubble,
let's fight that fire.

47
00:04:04,461 --> 00:04:05,680
Hoses on!

48
00:04:09,205 --> 00:04:10,946
Help! Up here!
Help!

49
00:04:10,989 --> 00:04:12,426
We're up here!

50
00:04:12,469 --> 00:04:15,559
My name's Zuma
and I'll be your rescue pup.

51
00:04:17,561 --> 00:04:20,651
All right!
Oh, thank goodness.

52
00:04:20,695 --> 00:04:23,437
It's time for you dudes
to ride the slide.

53
00:04:24,829 --> 00:04:26,396
Whoo-hoo!

54
00:04:26,440 --> 00:04:27,571
Whoa!

55
00:04:28,485 --> 00:04:29,617
Oh!

56
00:04:32,097 --> 00:04:33,098
Whoo!

57
00:04:34,404 --> 00:04:36,667
<i>All right, pups,</i>
<i>it's showtime!</i>

58
00:04:40,410 --> 00:04:42,934
Man, this video is fire!

59
00:04:42,978 --> 00:04:46,155
Dustin, get off your phone
and evacuate.

60
00:04:46,198 --> 00:04:48,766
Oh. Gotta go.
Like and subscribe.

61
00:04:48,810 --> 00:04:50,942
Hup! Whoo-hoo!

62
00:04:52,596 --> 00:04:53,641
That's everyone.

63
00:04:53,684 --> 00:04:55,077
Whoo-hoo!

64
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:57,079
<i>Nice work, Zuma.</i>

65
00:04:57,122 --> 00:04:59,560
The cat!
Hey, where's Mr. Fluffy Butt?

66
00:04:59,603 --> 00:05:02,084
He must still be onboard.

67
00:05:02,127 --> 00:05:05,174
Mr. Fluffy Butt!

68
00:05:05,217 --> 00:05:07,524
Pups, we've got a cat onboard.

69
00:05:07,568 --> 00:05:09,526
It's always a cat.

70
00:05:09,570 --> 00:05:11,702
Stuck in a tree,
stuck in a boat...

71
00:05:11,746 --> 00:05:13,400
Don't worry. I'm on it.

72
00:05:28,328 --> 00:05:31,505
Okay, Marshall.
No clumsiness, no mistakes.

73
00:05:39,730 --> 00:05:43,299
Here, kitty,
kitty, kitty! Hello!

74
00:05:43,343 --> 00:05:45,345
Mr. Fluffy Butt!

75
00:05:45,388 --> 00:05:48,043
Kitty, where are you?

76
00:05:57,661 --> 00:06:00,360
Looks like we're gonna have
to do this the hard way.

77
00:06:00,403 --> 00:06:01,622
Fire axes!

78
00:06:08,368 --> 00:06:09,847
I found the kitty.

79
00:06:09,891 --> 00:06:13,111
He's actually pretty cute.
For a cat.

80
00:06:16,637 --> 00:06:18,247
<i>Marshall,</i>
<i>your exit is blocked.</i>

81
00:06:18,290 --> 00:06:20,205
<i>You're gonna have to find</i>
<i>another way out.</i>

82
00:06:20,249 --> 00:06:21,163
Copy that.

83
00:06:26,081 --> 00:06:27,387
Sorry about this, kitty.

84
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:38,746
Oh, no!

85
00:06:38,789 --> 00:06:40,051
Come on, man.

86
00:06:40,095 --> 00:06:41,183
Where are they?

87
00:06:41,226 --> 00:06:42,489
No...
Oh, no.

88
00:06:45,056 --> 00:06:46,406
Yeah!

89
00:06:46,449 --> 00:06:48,973
That wasn't so bad,
was it, kitty?

90
00:06:51,759 --> 00:06:54,283
Come to mommy.
Come to mommy.

91
00:06:54,326 --> 00:06:57,852
Oh, my baby. Mwah.

92
00:06:57,895 --> 00:07:00,637
Ugh. Are you sure
that's Mr. Fluffy Butt?

93
00:07:01,943 --> 00:07:03,510
Don't worry.

94
00:07:03,553 --> 00:07:06,251
His butt will fluff up again
as soon as he dries off.

95
00:07:07,992 --> 00:07:11,518
Loop, swoop, and pull.

96
00:07:11,561 --> 00:07:13,998
All right,
the hitch is hooked!

97
00:07:14,042 --> 00:07:15,435
Don't worry, kids.

98
00:07:15,478 --> 00:07:17,828
Captain Turbot is the O.G.
of the high seas.

99
00:07:17,872 --> 00:07:20,004
He'll have us back
to land in no time.

100
00:07:20,048 --> 00:07:21,571
You know it!

101
00:07:21,615 --> 00:07:23,355
Goodbye, Cap'n Turbot!
Goodbye!

102
00:07:23,399 --> 00:07:24,879
Farewell, friends!
Bye!

103
00:07:24,922 --> 00:07:27,185
See you later!
Stay cool, little doggies!

104
00:07:27,229 --> 00:07:28,883
Bye, Mr. Fluffy Butt!

105
00:07:28,926 --> 00:07:32,277
Nice work, Marshall.
That was a perfect rescue.

106
00:07:32,321 --> 00:07:33,453
What can I say?

107
00:07:33,496 --> 00:07:35,890
Rescue pups
don't make mistakes.

108
00:07:40,198 --> 00:07:42,549
Looks like we're heading
into some weather.

109
00:07:42,592 --> 00:07:43,854
Buckle up, pups.

110
00:07:51,775 --> 00:07:54,082
Whoa!

111
00:07:54,125 --> 00:07:56,040
Whoa!

112
00:07:56,084 --> 00:07:58,390
Isn't this fun?

113
00:07:58,434 --> 00:08:01,872
I think
I'm more of a land mammal.

114
00:08:13,318 --> 00:08:15,146
Switch on the fog lights!

115
00:08:15,190 --> 00:08:16,887
Switching on fog lights.

116
00:08:26,636 --> 00:08:27,724
Ryder,

117
00:08:27,768 --> 00:08:29,683
we're drifting off course.

118
00:08:29,726 --> 00:08:33,208
I'm flying blind out here!
The instruments are going crazy.

119
00:08:33,251 --> 00:08:35,340
That's comforting.

120
00:08:35,384 --> 00:08:37,560
Wait, what is that?

121
00:08:38,213 --> 00:08:39,562
What on earth?

122
00:08:42,260 --> 00:08:44,262
Oh, no. No. No, no, no!

123
00:08:45,307 --> 00:08:46,656
Brace for impact!

124
00:08:51,792 --> 00:08:53,533
Whoa!

125
00:09:08,809 --> 00:09:09,897
Ugh.

126
00:09:11,333 --> 00:09:12,639
Ugh.

127
00:09:24,564 --> 00:09:28,742
This doesn't make any sense.
There's no island on the map.

128
00:09:28,785 --> 00:09:30,874
I guess it's time
to update the map.

129
00:09:32,093 --> 00:09:34,443
So what do
we do now?

130
00:09:34,486 --> 00:09:36,880
We've got
to explore the island.

131
00:09:36,924 --> 00:09:38,055
Marshall's
right.

132
00:09:38,099 --> 00:09:40,014
But if we're going
into that jungle,

133
00:09:40,057 --> 00:09:41,798
we need to suit up
for the job.

134
00:09:43,408 --> 00:09:44,540
<i>All right, pups,</i>

135
00:09:44,584 --> 00:09:46,673
<i>these are</i>
<i>your new survival suits.</i>

136
00:09:46,716 --> 00:09:49,763
<i>They've got</i>
<i>everything you need</i> <i>to stay alive in the jungle.</i>

137
00:09:49,806 --> 00:09:51,503
<i>Protection from the elements.</i>

138
00:09:51,547 --> 00:09:52,983
<i>Safety gear for climbing.</i>

139
00:09:53,027 --> 00:09:55,029
<i>Built-in floatation devices.</i>

140
00:09:55,072 --> 00:09:58,554
<i>Flashlights, compass</i>
<i>and G.P.S.</i>

141
00:09:58,598 --> 00:10:00,600
<i>Whatever this island</i>
<i>throws at us,</i>

142
00:10:00,643 --> 00:10:01,949
<i>we'll be prepared.</i>

143
00:10:05,909 --> 00:10:07,911
Ready for action,
Ryder, sir!

144
00:10:19,357 --> 00:10:21,664
This place
is amazing.

145
00:10:21,708 --> 00:10:23,927
Everything
is so huge.

146
00:10:25,015 --> 00:10:26,364
Let's climb
to the top of that cliff

147
00:10:26,408 --> 00:10:27,757
and get a lay of the land.

148
00:10:42,859 --> 00:10:43,730
Ugh.

149
00:10:43,773 --> 00:10:46,254
Wow. Look at that view!

150
00:10:54,479 --> 00:10:55,829
Dudes.

151
00:10:55,872 --> 00:10:57,657
It's incredible.

152
00:10:57,700 --> 00:11:00,747
And I've got
the best seat in the house.

153
00:11:00,790 --> 00:11:02,052
Whoa.

154
00:11:09,886 --> 00:11:11,322
I'm okay!

155
00:11:11,366 --> 00:11:13,890
Marshall!

156
00:11:16,371 --> 00:11:18,025
Marshall!

157
00:11:18,068 --> 00:11:20,680
What? I said I'm okay.
It's kind of my thing.

158
00:11:20,723 --> 00:11:22,594
I crash into something,
then I pop back up

159
00:11:22,638 --> 00:11:23,857
and say, "I'm okay!"

160
00:11:23,900 --> 00:11:24,945
People seem to like it.

161
00:11:24,988 --> 00:11:26,947
Marshall, run!

162
00:11:29,906 --> 00:11:32,561
What on earth
is that thing?!

163
00:11:38,741 --> 00:11:40,612
Come on! Go, go, go!

164
00:11:45,052 --> 00:11:46,793
Run!

165
00:11:46,836 --> 00:11:49,056
I am running!

166
00:11:49,099 --> 00:11:53,016
I'm a bulldog, this is as fast
as I can go!

167
00:11:53,060 --> 00:11:55,062
Is that a dinosaur?

168
00:11:55,105 --> 00:11:56,933
I thought those things
were extinct!

169
00:12:08,858 --> 00:12:10,773
Don't eat me! Don't eat me!

170
00:12:10,817 --> 00:12:12,209
Marshall!

171
00:12:34,579 --> 00:12:37,017
Get out of here,
you old cranky pants!

172
00:12:47,157 --> 00:12:48,898
You woke her up, didn't you?

173
00:12:48,942 --> 00:12:50,944
Wha-- W-What?

174
00:12:50,987 --> 00:12:52,336
Don't take it personally.

175
00:12:52,380 --> 00:12:55,557
That Spinosaurus is always
cranky after her nap.

176
00:12:58,690 --> 00:13:01,041
Boy, is it good to see
some other pups!

177
00:13:01,084 --> 00:13:02,869
It's just been me
and the dinosaurs

178
00:13:02,912 --> 00:13:05,045
for the last
two and a half years.

179
00:13:07,569 --> 00:13:10,702
Oh, how rude of me! I'm Rex.

180
00:13:10,746 --> 00:13:12,617
And this is Timmy the T-Rex.

181
00:13:16,012 --> 00:13:18,232
Timmy is t-t-terrifying.

182
00:13:18,275 --> 00:13:19,973
No, he's not.

183
00:13:20,016 --> 00:13:21,713
You're not terrifying.

184
00:13:21,757 --> 00:13:24,586
You're a good boy,
aren't you, buddy?

185
00:13:24,629 --> 00:13:27,110
Yeah, you're a good boy.

186
00:13:32,594 --> 00:13:35,162
H-How are there
dinosaurs here?

187
00:13:35,205 --> 00:13:38,339
How-- How are you here?
What's going on?

188
00:13:38,382 --> 00:13:40,602
I'm sure you got
a lot of questions.

189
00:13:40,645 --> 00:13:42,169
Why don't you let me
show you around,

190
00:13:42,212 --> 00:13:45,085
and I'll do my best
to answer as many as I can.

191
00:13:49,437 --> 00:13:51,047
I've been stranded
on this island

192
00:13:51,091 --> 00:13:53,528
since I fell overboard
during a storm.

193
00:13:53,571 --> 00:13:55,530
The first time
I saw a dinosaur,

194
00:13:55,573 --> 00:13:57,706
I almost jumped out of my fur.

195
00:13:57,749 --> 00:13:59,534
But they're actually
really friendly

196
00:13:59,577 --> 00:14:00,709
when you get to know them.

197
00:14:04,191 --> 00:14:05,714
Come on, follow me.

198
00:14:07,803 --> 00:14:08,630
Ha!

199
00:14:14,114 --> 00:14:15,506
Whoa!

200
00:14:15,550 --> 00:14:17,508
He is so cool.

201
00:14:17,552 --> 00:14:20,250
The pup's got moves,
no doubt about it.

202
00:14:25,081 --> 00:14:27,475
Whoa--

203
00:14:27,518 --> 00:14:30,260
Wait, whoa, whoa--
Whoa! Whoa, whoa, whoa!

204
00:14:31,827 --> 00:14:33,873
Marshall!

205
00:14:33,916 --> 00:14:35,875
Sorry about that.

206
00:14:35,918 --> 00:14:39,226
In case you haven't guessed,
I'm the clumsy pup.

207
00:14:39,269 --> 00:14:41,141
It's all good.
Keep trying.

208
00:14:41,184 --> 00:14:44,187
Everybody makes mistakes
when they're learning something new.

209
00:14:45,145 --> 00:14:46,363
Whoa. Look!

210
00:14:53,240 --> 00:14:55,285
Oh! Hello.

211
00:14:55,329 --> 00:14:56,678
Ah!

212
00:14:56,721 --> 00:14:59,115
Oh-- Uh...

213
00:15:01,639 --> 00:15:03,728
They're just shy.

214
00:15:03,772 --> 00:15:05,339
They'll get used
to you soon enough.

215
00:15:06,079 --> 00:15:07,776
Okay, this is me.

216
00:15:19,266 --> 00:15:23,096
Whoa. Rex,
you built all this?

217
00:15:23,139 --> 00:15:27,143
Yep. It's taken me
two years, a hundred and forty-seven days,

218
00:15:27,187 --> 00:15:28,884
and I'm almost done.

219
00:15:44,030 --> 00:15:46,815
Whoa! Whoa.

220
00:15:51,994 --> 00:15:53,256
All aboard.

221
00:15:53,822 --> 00:15:54,649
Hup.

222
00:15:57,478 --> 00:15:59,175
Oh! Whoa--
Whoa, whoa.

223
00:16:00,829 --> 00:16:02,091
Whoa!

224
00:16:04,702 --> 00:16:06,095
Whoo!

225
00:16:29,075 --> 00:16:30,641
Thanks for the lift, Nellie!

226
00:16:35,168 --> 00:16:37,039
Hey!

227
00:16:41,130 --> 00:16:44,177
It was always my dream
to build my own treehouse.

228
00:16:44,220 --> 00:16:47,658
When I got stranded out here,
I finally got the chance.

229
00:16:49,660 --> 00:16:51,010
Whoa!

230
00:16:51,662 --> 00:16:53,925
This is incredible!

231
00:16:53,969 --> 00:16:57,059
It's all made
out of stuff I found on the island.

232
00:16:57,103 --> 00:16:58,974
It's amazing how much nature
will give you

233
00:16:59,018 --> 00:17:00,454
if you know where to look.

234
00:17:01,629 --> 00:17:04,023
Welcome to my home sweet home.

235
00:17:04,066 --> 00:17:05,850
It doesn't have
air conditioning,

236
00:17:05,894 --> 00:17:08,157
a big screen TV or Wi-Fi...

237
00:17:09,680 --> 00:17:10,986
...but it does the trick.

238
00:17:11,421 --> 00:17:13,206
Wow!

239
00:17:13,249 --> 00:17:17,166
Dude, this is the coolest
treehouse in the world!

240
00:17:17,210 --> 00:17:20,517
It's glamping. I could
totally get behind this.

241
00:17:20,561 --> 00:17:22,737
Plus, being up this high
must give you some privacy

242
00:17:22,780 --> 00:17:24,043
from all the dinosaurs.

243
00:17:24,086 --> 00:17:25,261
Ah!

244
00:17:26,219 --> 00:17:27,655
Or maybe not.

245
00:17:31,311 --> 00:17:33,791
If you really want to see
Dino Island,

246
00:17:33,835 --> 00:17:35,750
there's only one way
to do it.

247
00:17:37,578 --> 00:17:40,320
Do you want to go
for a ride?

248
00:17:40,363 --> 00:17:42,409
<i></i>

249
00:17:42,452 --> 00:17:44,759
<i>♪ Something about you</i>
<i>Got me</i>

250
00:17:46,587 --> 00:17:47,762
<i>♪ Like lightning struck</i>

251
00:17:47,805 --> 00:17:49,111
<i>♪ My body</i>

252
00:17:49,155 --> 00:17:50,895
<i>♪ Tell the room</i>
<i>Get out the way</i>

253
00:17:50,939 --> 00:17:51,983
Yeah!

254
00:17:52,027 --> 00:17:53,159
<i>♪ We are made of broken pieces</i>

255
00:17:53,202 --> 00:17:55,291
<i>♪ But that's how</i>
<i>The love gets in</i>

256
00:17:55,335 --> 00:17:57,641
Whoo-hoo!

257
00:17:57,685 --> 00:17:59,426
<i>♪ You're under my skin</i>

258
00:17:59,469 --> 00:18:01,906
Check it out! Triceratops!

259
00:18:03,473 --> 00:18:06,128
<i>♪ Ooh, if you're feeling</i>
<i>The love go deeper</i>

