493
00:30:56,855 --> 00:30:59,335
Well, I'll be.

494
00:31:05,689 --> 00:31:07,561
Look at the size
of that thing.

495
00:31:14,481 --> 00:31:16,352
Ugh, well,
we don't have all day.

496
00:31:16,396 --> 00:31:18,746
Get that thing
out of the way.

497
00:31:18,789 --> 00:31:21,096
Stand back. I got this.

498
00:31:31,150 --> 00:31:32,803
What are you doing?

499
00:31:32,847 --> 00:31:36,764
That is my dinosaur call.
I'm trying to get his attention.

500
00:31:36,807 --> 00:31:39,332
Aw, isn't that cute?

501
00:31:39,375 --> 00:31:41,595
Not gonna work, though.
Out of my way!

502
00:31:41,638 --> 00:31:44,250
Coming through!

503
00:31:47,253 --> 00:31:48,994
What do you think
you're doing?

504
00:31:49,037 --> 00:31:52,519
I'm not letting
this Cretaceous cretin stand in my way.

505
00:31:59,613 --> 00:32:00,962
Move it!

506
00:32:01,006 --> 00:32:03,573
Get out of my way,
I've got places to be!

507
00:32:03,617 --> 00:32:05,053
Scoot! Shoo! Vamoose!

508
00:32:24,464 --> 00:32:25,769
Whoa.

509
00:32:25,813 --> 00:32:29,208
What?! That wasn't my fault.
He tripped on his own.

510
00:32:29,251 --> 00:32:30,774
You saw it, right, kitties?

511
00:32:44,658 --> 00:32:45,876
Okay, Rhubarb,

512
00:32:45,920 --> 00:32:48,140
we've got to work
on that roar of yours.

513
00:32:48,183 --> 00:32:49,532
You're a T-Rex.

514
00:32:49,576 --> 00:32:51,795
You should have a big, loud,

515
00:32:51,839 --> 00:32:54,146
commanding roar!

516
00:32:54,189 --> 00:32:57,192
Here, do what I do.
Put your feet apart like this.

517
00:32:58,411 --> 00:33:00,108
Now stand up straight.

518
00:33:01,196 --> 00:33:02,893
Chest forward.

519
00:33:03,894 --> 00:33:06,071
But keep your tail
in the air.

520
00:33:06,114 --> 00:33:08,421
Take a deep breath.

521
00:33:10,466 --> 00:33:12,512
Now... roar!

522
00:33:19,388 --> 00:33:24,393
Okay, not bad.
It was a good start.

523
00:33:24,437 --> 00:33:27,396
You'll get there.
You just need to stick with it.

524
00:33:29,920 --> 00:33:31,835
Hey, Heidi.
How's it going out there?

525
00:33:31,879 --> 00:33:34,490
<i>Ryder!</i>
<i>There's a Brachiosaurus</i> <i>in trouble!</i>

526
00:33:37,276 --> 00:33:38,407
Where are you?

527
00:33:38,451 --> 00:33:40,105
<i>We're on the far side</i>
<i>of the island.</i>

528
00:33:40,148 --> 00:33:41,715
<i>I'm sending you</i>
<i>the coordinates now.</i>

529
00:33:41,758 --> 00:33:43,151
We're on our way.

530
00:33:43,717 --> 00:33:44,848
Come on, pups!

531
00:33:44,892 --> 00:33:47,677
No dino's too big,
no pup's too small.

532
00:33:51,072 --> 00:33:52,900
<i>Pups,</i>
<i>get ready to launch.</i>

533
00:34:17,098 --> 00:34:18,926
Ready for launch!

534
00:34:18,969 --> 00:34:20,014
Marshall, go!

535
00:34:32,461 --> 00:34:34,202
Skye, go!

536
00:34:43,124 --> 00:34:44,125
Zuma, go!

537
00:34:48,260 --> 00:34:49,609
Rocky, go!

538
00:34:51,828 --> 00:34:53,091
Rubble, go!

539
00:34:59,706 --> 00:35:01,577
Chase, go!

540
00:35:19,117 --> 00:35:20,901
Oh, thank goodness
you're here.

541
00:35:21,684 --> 00:35:22,685
What happened?

542
00:35:22,729 --> 00:35:24,687
I don't know.
He must have slipped.

543
00:35:34,697 --> 00:35:36,046
We don't have much time!

544
00:35:36,090 --> 00:35:38,614
Chase, Rocky,
let's get him strapped in.

545
00:35:38,658 --> 00:35:39,746
You got it, Ryder!

546
00:35:41,095 --> 00:35:42,662
Dropping in.

547
00:35:46,535 --> 00:35:48,058
Let's do this.

548
00:35:55,022 --> 00:35:56,763
Marshall, I need you
to use your winch

549
00:35:56,806 --> 00:35:58,721
to pull that
Brachiosaurus out of there.

550
00:35:58,765 --> 00:36:01,246
I'm on it!
Stabilizers down.

551
00:36:04,988 --> 00:36:06,164
Here we go.

552
00:36:12,605 --> 00:36:14,389
Let's flip and clip.

553
00:36:18,001 --> 00:36:19,655
Deploying net.

554
00:36:25,574 --> 00:36:27,185
Here comes the hook!

555
00:36:28,969 --> 00:36:31,406
The Brachiosaurus
is secure.

556
00:36:31,450 --> 00:36:33,582
All right, Marshall,
haul him up.

557
00:36:33,626 --> 00:36:35,062
Copy that.

558
00:36:35,105 --> 00:36:37,499
Okay, Marshall,
no mistakes.

559
00:36:44,419 --> 00:36:46,334
Dino's on the move!

560
00:36:46,378 --> 00:36:48,554
Bringing him up
slow and steady.

561
00:37:01,044 --> 00:37:02,611
Something's stuck
in the winch!

562
00:37:04,570 --> 00:37:07,137
Hang on! I'll fix it.

563
00:37:14,144 --> 00:37:16,234
No, no. No, no, no, no!
No, no!

564
00:37:18,018 --> 00:37:18,932
Marshall!

565
00:37:27,941 --> 00:37:28,811
Look out!

566
00:37:28,855 --> 00:37:29,725
Whoa!

567
00:37:38,212 --> 00:37:39,474
My truck!

568
00:37:47,047 --> 00:37:48,440
Oh, no.

569
00:37:48,483 --> 00:37:50,529
How are we gonna get
that dino out now?

570
00:37:52,270 --> 00:37:53,967
What can we do to help?

571
00:37:58,667 --> 00:38:00,800
Everybody, grab a rope!

572
00:38:06,545 --> 00:38:09,809
Three, two, one,

573
00:38:09,852 --> 00:38:11,158
pull!

574
00:38:23,170 --> 00:38:24,214
It's stuck!

575
00:38:26,304 --> 00:38:27,566
Come on!

576
00:38:38,011 --> 00:38:39,404
It's working!

577
00:38:54,506 --> 00:38:56,029
Great work, team.

578
00:38:56,072 --> 00:38:57,726
Nicely done,
pups!

579
00:39:07,736 --> 00:39:10,348
You gotta watch
your step next time, big guy.

580
00:39:13,829 --> 00:39:16,484
He seems so steady
on his feet.

581
00:39:16,528 --> 00:39:18,573
I wonder what made him fall.

582
00:39:36,417 --> 00:39:37,331
We're here!

583
00:39:39,289 --> 00:39:40,682
Oh!

584
00:39:40,726 --> 00:39:41,988
Uh-huh?

585
00:39:47,994 --> 00:39:49,561
Stay behind me.

586
00:39:49,604 --> 00:39:52,868
Who knows
what kind of monsters are hiding in these shadows.

587
00:40:06,534 --> 00:40:09,189
Sorry, I-- I thought
it would be bigger.

588
00:40:09,232 --> 00:40:10,843
Don't worry.

589
00:40:10,886 --> 00:40:13,628
I'm not gonna tell anybody
you scream like that.

590
00:40:13,672 --> 00:40:17,632
Ooh. Check it out.
This is igneous rock.

591
00:40:17,676 --> 00:40:21,288
The whole island is sitting
on top of a giant volcano!

592
00:40:21,331 --> 00:40:22,985
A volcano.

593
00:40:23,029 --> 00:40:25,466
Not sure I like
the sound of that.

594
00:40:25,510 --> 00:40:26,772
It's nothing
to worry about.

595
00:40:26,815 --> 00:40:29,514
This baby's been dormant
for thousands of years.

596
00:40:29,557 --> 00:40:31,472
It's not waking up
for anybody.

597
00:40:31,516 --> 00:40:35,998
It's even sparklier
than it was on TV!

598
00:40:36,042 --> 00:40:37,739
I'm gonna be rich.

599
00:40:37,783 --> 00:40:39,349
No, filthy rich.

600
00:40:39,393 --> 00:40:42,788
No! Filthy, stinking rich!

601
00:40:44,398 --> 00:40:45,747
Mm!

602
00:40:45,791 --> 00:40:47,009
Ow!

603
00:40:47,053 --> 00:40:49,969
Get off me! Get off me!

604
00:40:50,012 --> 00:40:51,579
Ow!

605
00:40:51,623 --> 00:40:53,581
Don't worry,
I'll set some traps.

606
00:40:53,625 --> 00:40:55,931
Teach these bitey little
critters some manners.

607
00:40:58,368 --> 00:40:59,544
Everything's fine.

608
00:41:00,283 --> 00:41:02,547
Okay.

609
00:41:03,809 --> 00:41:05,811
Well, what are we
standing around for?

610
00:41:05,854 --> 00:41:07,290
Let's mine these diamonds

611
00:41:07,334 --> 00:41:09,423
and get out of here
before the PAW Patrol

612
00:41:09,467 --> 00:41:11,294
starts sniffing around.

613
00:41:14,602 --> 00:41:16,082
Ooh.

614
00:41:16,125 --> 00:41:18,476
That's not good.

615
00:41:21,783 --> 00:41:24,525
We're going to need
a little more power.

616
00:41:27,702 --> 00:41:31,184
Hey, Humdinger!
You sure you can handle that thing?

617
00:41:31,227 --> 00:41:33,839
What? I can't hear you!

618
00:41:46,460 --> 00:41:48,027
Ha, ha, ha.

619
00:41:48,070 --> 00:41:50,464
You little lizards
think this is funny?

620
00:41:50,508 --> 00:41:52,945
I'll give you something
to laugh about.

621
00:41:53,641 --> 00:41:56,035
Assemble the drill!

622
00:41:56,078 --> 00:41:58,428
Now, that's what
I'm talking about.

623
00:41:58,472 --> 00:42:01,780
Let's get this party started!

624
00:42:27,632 --> 00:42:30,373
You really smashed
that sucker up good, didn't you?

625
00:42:30,896 --> 00:42:32,506
Yep.

626
00:42:32,550 --> 00:42:35,509
Eh! Don't worry about it.
Mistakes happen.

627
00:42:35,553 --> 00:42:38,512
Rescue pups aren't
supposed to make mistakes.

628
00:42:41,646 --> 00:42:44,605
That's not true.
Everybody makes mistakes.

629
00:42:45,171 --> 00:42:46,912
Not you.

630
00:42:46,955 --> 00:42:48,130
Are you kidding?

631
00:42:48,174 --> 00:42:50,524
I make more mistakes
than anyone.

632
00:42:51,438 --> 00:42:53,527
You do?

633
00:42:53,571 --> 00:42:56,182
You look up
and see a finished treehouse.

634
00:42:56,225 --> 00:42:57,618
But what you don't see

635
00:42:57,662 --> 00:43:00,621
is all the mistakes
it took to get there.

636
00:43:00,665 --> 00:43:03,493
Making mistakes is how
you learn and get better.

637
00:43:04,190 --> 00:43:05,670
Well, that...

638
00:43:05,713 --> 00:43:07,628
and never giving up.

639
00:43:12,546 --> 00:43:14,417
All right, let her rip!

640
00:43:17,986 --> 00:43:20,206
Hang on, kitties.

641
00:43:28,649 --> 00:43:30,956
Whoa! Whoa!

642
00:43:30,999 --> 00:43:32,522
Whoa!

643
00:43:32,566 --> 00:43:33,828
Wow--

644
00:43:42,271 --> 00:43:45,492
What kind of cut-rate
mining equipment is this?!

645
00:43:45,535 --> 00:43:48,713
Hey, it's not my fault.
The diamond is too hard.

646
00:43:48,756 --> 00:43:50,628
I've never seen
anything like it.

647
00:43:50,671 --> 00:43:52,064
So, what do we do?

648
00:43:52,630 --> 00:43:53,674
When in doubt...

649
00:43:53,718 --> 00:43:56,111
we blast it out!

650
00:43:57,678 --> 00:44:00,028
Blast it out,
blast it out, blast it out!

651
00:44:00,072 --> 00:44:03,858
I said we blast it out,
blast it out, blast it out!

652
00:44:03,902 --> 00:44:05,077
Whoo-hoo!

653
00:44:07,470 --> 00:44:09,342
Everybody stand back.

654
00:44:09,385 --> 00:44:12,388
Oh, oh, oh! Can I press
the dynamite plunger thingy?

655
00:44:12,432 --> 00:44:14,303
Can I? Please?

656
00:44:16,654 --> 00:44:18,046
Fine.

657
00:44:18,090 --> 00:44:20,222
Just stop making that face.
You're freaking me out!

658
00:44:20,266 --> 00:44:22,137
I've wanted to do this

659
00:44:22,181 --> 00:44:24,662
ever since I started
watching cartoons.

660
00:44:24,705 --> 00:44:27,273


661
00:44:43,332 --> 00:44:45,726
I love it
when it goes boom!

662
00:44:48,686 --> 00:44:50,122
Ooh.

663
00:44:50,165 --> 00:44:51,558
Wow!

664
00:44:51,601 --> 00:44:55,823
It worked!
It worked!

665
00:44:55,867 --> 00:44:58,217
We're gonna need
more dynamite.

666
00:44:58,260 --> 00:45:00,610
A lot more dynamite.

667
00:45:10,751 --> 00:45:11,970
Huh?

668
00:45:18,672 --> 00:45:20,239
What is that?

669
00:45:20,282 --> 00:45:22,110
Do you guys hear
that sound?

670
00:45:23,372 --> 00:45:24,765
It's my stomach.

671
00:45:24,809 --> 00:45:27,159
Those baby dinosaurs
ate all my pup treats.

672
00:45:29,857 --> 00:45:32,077
Somebody get
this guy a snack!

673
00:45:34,035 --> 00:45:34,949
Whoa!

674
00:45:36,081 --> 00:45:38,170
It's a stampede!

675
00:45:38,213 --> 00:45:39,475
Whoa!

676
00:45:50,617 --> 00:45:52,967
They're heading
straight for the geology camp!

677
00:45:55,665 --> 00:45:57,885
Come on, pups,
let's roll!

678
00:46:00,670 --> 00:46:03,673
I can't go on the rescue.
I've got no truck!

679
00:46:19,515 --> 00:46:21,779
Anybody need a ride?

680
00:46:23,345 --> 00:46:25,434
Come on, Rhubarb,
let's go!

681
00:46:32,833 --> 00:46:34,226
Our hypothesis

682
00:46:34,269 --> 00:46:37,533
is that lava tubes running
underneath the dormant volcano

683
00:46:37,577 --> 00:46:39,057
kept the island warm enough

684
00:46:39,100 --> 00:46:42,451
for these dinosaurs
to survive the Ice Age.

685
00:46:42,495 --> 00:46:44,149
And cut!

686
00:46:44,192 --> 00:46:45,846
We got it.

687
00:46:47,195 --> 00:46:48,283
Take cover!

688
00:46:48,327 --> 00:46:49,719
Whoa!

689
00:46:49,763 --> 00:46:51,765
Oh, look out!

690
00:46:51,809 --> 00:46:54,855
Help, help!
It's a stampede!

691
00:46:54,899 --> 00:46:55,725
Whoa!

692
00:47:10,001 --> 00:47:12,351
Ryder! Someone's caught
in the stampede!

693
00:47:13,700 --> 00:47:15,615
Copy that.
We're on our way.

694
00:47:18,009 --> 00:47:20,011
There she is!

695
00:47:20,054 --> 00:47:21,751
Help, over here!

696
00:47:21,795 --> 00:47:23,057
Hang on!

697
00:47:23,101 --> 00:47:24,232
I'm going in.

698
00:47:27,496 --> 00:47:30,673
There's too many dinos.
We can't get in there!

699
00:47:30,717 --> 00:47:32,371
Well, who's gonna save her?

700
00:47:33,763 --> 00:47:36,114
Come on, Rhubarb,
it's up to us!

701
00:47:36,157 --> 00:47:37,028
Hi-yah!

702
00:47:41,771 --> 00:47:42,860
Hi-yah!

703
00:47:43,730 --> 00:47:45,471
Yeah! Marshall!

704
00:47:48,169 --> 00:47:51,738
I can see her!
She's just up ahead!

705
00:47:51,781 --> 00:47:54,306
Marshall,
I'm dropping a rescue line.

706
00:47:59,572 --> 00:48:02,401
Come on, Rhubarb,
we've got to get in close!

707
00:48:02,444 --> 00:48:04,969
I can't hang on!

708
00:48:05,012 --> 00:48:06,971
Steady, steady.

709
00:48:07,014 --> 00:48:07,885
Help!

710
00:48:07,928 --> 00:48:09,190
Now!

711
00:48:12,585 --> 00:48:15,153
It's gonna be okay!

712
00:48:15,196 --> 00:48:17,285
I can't
hang on anymore!

713
00:48:17,329 --> 00:48:20,549
I just need you to hang on
for five more seconds.

714
00:48:20,593 --> 00:48:22,116
You can let go in five...

715
00:48:23,248 --> 00:48:24,249
...four...

716
00:48:25,163 --> 00:48:26,860
three...

717
00:48:26,904 --> 00:48:27,861
...two...

718
00:48:30,037 --> 00:48:31,647
...one!

719
00:48:35,129 --> 00:48:36,478
Yeah!

720
00:48:39,873 --> 00:48:41,527
Did you see that?!

721
00:48:41,570 --> 00:48:43,703
<i>Got her.</i>
<i>Nice moves, Marshall.</i>

722
00:48:43,746 --> 00:48:45,923
<i>Now get out of there.</i>

723
00:48:49,491 --> 00:48:51,102
You ready, buddy?

724
00:48:52,059 --> 00:48:53,365
Let's do this.

725
00:48:53,408 --> 00:48:55,062
Oof!

726
00:48:57,108 --> 00:48:58,457
Oof.

727
00:48:58,500 --> 00:49:00,589
No! Rhubarb!

728
00:49:13,472 --> 00:49:14,777
Marshall?

729
00:49:16,649 --> 00:49:17,824
Marshall?

730
00:49:23,438 --> 00:49:26,006
You took a pretty hard fall
out there.

731
00:49:26,050 --> 00:49:28,226
The good thing
is nothing's broken.

732
00:49:29,314 --> 00:49:30,880
Where's Rhubarb?

733
00:49:32,360 --> 00:49:33,971
We don't know.

734
00:49:34,014 --> 00:49:35,798
He got lost
in the stampede.

735
00:49:35,842 --> 00:49:37,322
I have to find him.

736
00:49:37,365 --> 00:49:40,586
You need to rest.
The team's out looking for him now.

737
00:49:41,369 --> 00:49:43,110
Rhubarb could be hurt.

738
00:49:46,984 --> 00:49:48,637
This is all my fault.

739
00:49:49,725 --> 00:49:52,685
No, it's not.
It was an accident.

740
00:49:52,728 --> 00:49:55,949
Accidents seem to happen
a lot around me.

741
00:49:55,993 --> 00:49:58,517
I used to be funny
being the clumsy pup.

742
00:49:58,560 --> 00:50:00,214
I'd fall down
and say "I'm okay"

743
00:50:00,258 --> 00:50:02,216
and everything would be fine.

744
00:50:02,260 --> 00:50:03,783
But now it's not fine.

745
00:50:05,306 --> 00:50:07,656
I keep making mistakes.

746
00:50:07,700 --> 00:50:10,137
I almost got eaten
by a dinosaur.

747
00:50:10,181 --> 00:50:11,965
I wrecked my truck.

748
00:50:12,009 --> 00:50:13,836
And this time,
when I messed up,

749
00:50:14,620 --> 00:50:17,188
I hurt my friend.

750
00:50:17,231 --> 00:50:20,234
Sometimes I think
you'd all be better off

751
00:50:20,278 --> 00:50:22,323
without a clumsy pup like me.

752
00:50:22,367 --> 00:50:24,151
Don't say that.

753
00:50:24,195 --> 00:50:26,458
You're only focusing
on your mistakes.

754
00:50:26,501 --> 00:50:28,721
Think of all
the good things you've done.

755
00:50:30,810 --> 00:50:32,855
Do you remember
the first time we met?

756
00:50:41,081 --> 00:50:43,562
Welcome to
the PAW Patrol tryouts.

757
00:50:43,605 --> 00:50:46,478
Good luck out there, pups.
Let's see what you can do.

758
00:50:59,186 --> 00:51:00,100
Whoa!

759
00:51:11,807 --> 00:51:13,548
Whoa!

760
00:51:15,072 --> 00:51:15,898
Hup.

761
00:51:16,812 --> 00:51:18,597
Yeah-- Uh-- Uh!

762
00:51:24,124 --> 00:51:24,994
Oof.

763
00:51:39,792 --> 00:51:42,229
Ryder,
come see this.

764
00:51:55,547 --> 00:51:56,548
Whoa.

765
00:51:56,591 --> 00:51:57,810
Whoa!

766
00:52:02,336 --> 00:52:04,730
I can do this.

767
00:52:09,126 --> 00:52:10,649
<i>I didn't</i>
<i>pick you because</i>

768
00:52:10,692 --> 00:52:12,433
<i>you never made mistakes.</i>

769
00:52:17,525 --> 00:52:19,571
<i>I picked you</i>
<i>because you're the pup</i>

770
00:52:19,614 --> 00:52:21,138
<i>that never gives up.</i>

771
00:52:40,896 --> 00:52:43,899
I don't need you
to be perfect.

772
00:52:43,943 --> 00:52:47,207
I just need you to give it
everything you've got.

773
00:52:47,251 --> 00:52:49,166
Can you do that
for me?

774
00:52:49,209 --> 00:52:51,211
You can count
on me, Ryder.

775
00:52:58,653 --> 00:53:01,569
Is he okay?
Did you find Rhubarb?

776
00:53:01,613 --> 00:53:03,528
No, not yet.

777
00:53:03,571 --> 00:53:06,487
It's too dark
out there. We can't see a thing.

778
00:53:07,401 --> 00:53:09,360
But we're not giving up.

779
00:53:09,403 --> 00:53:11,710
We'll start the search again
first thing in the morning.

780
00:53:50,270 --> 00:53:52,794
Hey!
Where are you going?

781
00:53:52,838 --> 00:53:54,753
I'm going
to find Rhubarb.

782
00:53:54,796 --> 00:53:56,537
It's pitch black
out there.

783
00:53:56,581 --> 00:53:59,366
There's no way you're gonna
find him in the dark.

784
00:53:59,410 --> 00:54:02,761
I have to try. I can't just
sit around till morning.

785
00:54:02,804 --> 00:54:04,980
The jungle's no joke
at night.

786
00:54:05,024 --> 00:54:07,069
It's easy to get lost
out there.

787
00:54:07,940 --> 00:54:09,681
I'm not giving up on him.

788
00:54:20,605 --> 00:54:21,910
Rhubarb!

789
00:54:25,174 --> 00:54:27,176
Rhubarb!

790
00:54:29,004 --> 00:54:31,050
Rhubarb?

791
00:54:38,492 --> 00:54:40,755
Hello? Rhubarb?

792
00:54:54,856 --> 00:54:56,205
Rhubarb?!

793
00:54:56,641 --> 00:54:58,556
Rhubarb!

794
00:54:58,599 --> 00:55:00,645
Where are you?

795
00:55:05,084 --> 00:55:06,433
Rhubarb!

796
00:55:15,007 --> 00:55:16,313
I'm okay.

797
00:55:17,836 --> 00:55:20,055
Yeah, I'm okay.

798
00:55:29,848 --> 00:55:31,197
Whoa!

799
00:55:31,240 --> 00:55:33,330
What's going on?

800
00:55:33,373 --> 00:55:35,332
Get me out of here!

801
00:55:35,375 --> 00:55:37,334
Help!

802
00:55:39,727 --> 00:55:41,294
Hmm.

803
00:55:41,338 --> 00:55:43,296
Put them closer!
Pack it in there!

804
00:55:43,340 --> 00:55:46,386
It's gonna be
the Fourth of July!

805
00:55:46,430 --> 00:55:49,563
I think we've got
enough dynamite, boss.

806
00:55:49,607 --> 00:55:52,174
It's enough
when I say it's enough!

807
00:55:52,218 --> 00:55:54,220
Keep going!

808
00:55:54,263 --> 00:55:56,527
Hey!
Guess what.

809
00:55:56,570 --> 00:55:58,833
I caught
my first dinosaur.

810
00:55:59,660 --> 00:56:00,705
Humdinger!

811
00:56:00,748 --> 00:56:03,403
That's not a dinosaur.

812
00:56:03,447 --> 00:56:06,450
It's one of those dogs
from the PAW Patrol.

813
00:56:06,493 --> 00:56:07,581
There are
so many of them,

814
00:56:07,625 --> 00:56:09,496
I can never remember
their names.

815
00:56:09,540 --> 00:56:11,585
Oh, oh, oh!
That one's Marshall!

816
00:56:11,629 --> 00:56:13,848
He's my nephew's favorite!

817
00:56:15,502 --> 00:56:18,287
If I had known
you had a nephew that liked the PAW Patrol,

818
00:56:18,331 --> 00:56:20,202
I never would have hired you!

819
00:56:20,246 --> 00:56:21,726
What are you
doing here?

820
00:56:21,769 --> 00:56:23,554
Well,
we started out drilling,

821
00:56:23,597 --> 00:56:25,382
but now we've moved on
to blasting.

822
00:56:25,425 --> 00:56:27,079
Are you out of your mind?!

823
00:56:27,122 --> 00:56:28,863
That's a dormant volcano!

824
00:56:28,907 --> 00:56:30,387
If you set that thing off,

825
00:56:30,430 --> 00:56:32,824
you're going to destroy
the island.

826
00:56:32,867 --> 00:56:35,740
Well, I guess that's just
the cost of doing business.

827
00:56:35,783 --> 00:56:39,004
Keep an eye on this one.
Those pups are slippery.

828
00:56:39,047 --> 00:56:40,571
Don't let him
out of your sight.

829
00:56:40,614 --> 00:56:43,269
Don't worry.
He's not going anywhere.

830
00:56:51,625 --> 00:56:53,105
You won't get away
with this.

831
00:56:53,148 --> 00:56:54,585
"You won't
get away with this."

832
00:56:56,587 --> 00:56:59,677
I'm afraid it's you
who won't be getting away.

833
00:57:00,852 --> 00:57:02,375
That's all of it.

834
00:57:02,419 --> 00:57:04,725
We're officially
out of dynamite.

835
00:57:10,078 --> 00:57:11,906
Nice work, Marshall.

836
00:57:11,950 --> 00:57:14,779
You didn't find Rhubarb,
you got yourself caught,

837
00:57:14,822 --> 00:57:16,824
and now Humdinger's gonna
blow up the island

838
00:57:16,868 --> 00:57:19,479
while you're stuck here
doing nothing.

839
00:57:19,523 --> 00:57:22,003
So much for being the pup
who never gives up.

840
00:57:23,222 --> 00:57:25,311
Who said anything
about giving up?

841
00:57:26,312 --> 00:57:27,444
Rex?

842
00:57:27,487 --> 00:57:28,923
What are you doing here?

843
00:57:28,967 --> 00:57:31,752
I followed your trail.
And it's a good thing I did.

844
00:57:31,796 --> 00:57:32,971
Now let's get you
out of here.

845
00:57:34,363 --> 00:57:35,452
What about her?

846
00:57:37,715 --> 00:57:38,629
Heh.

847
00:57:38,672 --> 00:57:39,934
I'll handle it.

848
00:57:50,815 --> 00:57:52,120
What is this?

849
00:57:52,164 --> 00:57:54,949
A bone-shaped cookie?

850
00:57:58,344 --> 00:58:01,521
They love
those pup treats.

851
00:58:01,565 --> 00:58:03,567
Humdinger's got
the whole volcano wired

852
00:58:03,610 --> 00:58:04,742
with dynamite!

853
00:58:04,785 --> 00:58:06,787
You might want
to plug your ears!

854
00:58:06,831 --> 00:58:07,919
Wait, no, stop!

855
00:58:25,371 --> 00:58:26,328
Whoo-hoo!

856
00:58:31,508 --> 00:58:32,552
Whoa!

857
00:58:42,910 --> 00:58:46,044
Now that's what I call
having a blast!

858
00:58:50,657 --> 00:58:52,311
The volcano!

859
00:58:55,662 --> 00:58:57,925
We have to warn Ryder.
Come on!

860
00:59:14,115 --> 00:59:15,247
Ryder!
Ryder!

861
00:59:15,290 --> 00:59:17,902
Ryder!
Ryder!

862
00:59:17,945 --> 00:59:20,382
Marshall! Rex!
Where were you?

863
00:59:20,426 --> 00:59:21,558
Humdinger's here!

864
00:59:21,601 --> 00:59:23,081
Humdinger?!

865
00:59:23,124 --> 00:59:25,387
He just set off
a thousand sticks of dynamite

866
00:59:25,431 --> 00:59:26,780
on the side of the volcano.

867
00:59:33,395 --> 00:59:34,527
Whoa!

868
00:59:34,571 --> 00:59:36,398
What on earth?
Oh, no.

869
00:59:39,967 --> 00:59:42,491
Rhubarb's still out there!

870
00:59:42,535 --> 00:59:45,103
Look out!

871
00:59:45,146 --> 00:59:48,236
We've got to get
all the people and the dinosaurs to safety.

872
00:59:48,280 --> 00:59:50,151
We're on it!

873
00:59:50,195 --> 00:59:53,198
What about Rhubarb?
Don't worry. I'll find him.

874
00:59:53,241 --> 00:59:54,982
Then you're
gonna need this.

875
00:59:59,508 --> 01:00:02,033
My truck!
Meet us at the caverns.

876
01:00:05,645 --> 01:00:08,082
I'm fired up!

877
01:00:13,740 --> 01:00:14,872
Where's Timmy?

878
01:00:14,915 --> 01:00:16,395
When I was fixing
Marshall's truck,

879
01:00:16,438 --> 01:00:18,919
I made a few upgrades
to your ride, too.

880
01:00:26,013 --> 01:00:27,275
Whoa!

881
01:00:27,319 --> 01:00:30,539
Let's roll out!
We've got an island to save.

882
01:00:41,550 --> 01:00:45,032
This job is
much more dangerous than I thought it would be.

883
01:00:45,076 --> 01:00:46,164
Whoa!

884
01:00:53,562 --> 01:00:55,652
We've got to get
everyone to the caverns.

885
01:00:55,695 --> 01:00:57,784
It's the only place
we'll be safe.

886
01:00:57,828 --> 01:00:59,786
Come on!
Let's move it, people!

887
01:01:01,875 --> 01:01:03,964
Everybody on!

888
01:01:06,793 --> 01:01:09,404
Okay, go, go!

889
01:01:09,448 --> 01:01:11,189
Wait up!
Wait up!

890
01:01:21,416 --> 01:01:22,504
Over here!

891
01:01:22,548 --> 01:01:24,637
Help me get the big one.

892
01:01:24,681 --> 01:01:27,553
The bigger they are,
the more they're worth!

893
01:01:27,596 --> 01:01:30,208
The truck's full
of diamonds. We're already rich.

894
01:01:30,251 --> 01:01:31,688
Let's get out
of here, man!

895
01:01:31,731 --> 01:01:34,342
But look at the size
of this thing!

896
01:01:34,386 --> 01:01:37,345
You think there's
a lesson here about not being too greedy?

897
01:01:38,042 --> 01:01:40,044
No, I don't.

898
01:01:40,087 --> 01:01:41,436
Now get over here
and lift!

899
01:01:45,440 --> 01:01:48,443
Come on, you weaklings,
lift with your backs.

900
01:01:57,452 --> 01:01:59,411
Lift!

901
01:01:59,454 --> 01:02:01,587
Uh, we should really
get out of here.

902
01:02:01,630 --> 01:02:04,721
No! I am not leaving
this diamond.

903
01:02:07,811 --> 01:02:08,681
Huh?

904
01:02:08,725 --> 01:02:11,162
Oh!

905
01:02:19,648 --> 01:02:21,868
No!

906
01:02:29,136 --> 01:02:30,442
Hey, hey, hey!

907
01:02:30,485 --> 01:02:31,748
Come on,
little buddy.

908
01:02:31,791 --> 01:02:32,705
Come on.

909
01:02:32,749 --> 01:02:34,272
We got to get you
out of here.

910
01:02:38,842 --> 01:02:40,582
Come on now. Come on.

911
01:02:40,626 --> 01:02:41,758
Get down from that tree.

912
01:02:41,801 --> 01:02:42,976
No, no, no, no, no!
Get up in the tree!

913
01:02:43,020 --> 01:02:43,803
Get up in the tree!

914
01:03:01,429 --> 01:03:03,780
All right, Timmy,
I'm gonna grab them.

915
01:03:03,823 --> 01:03:06,260
Come on, little guys.
Hop on.

916
01:03:13,833 --> 01:03:15,617
I'm happy to give you a ride,

917
01:03:15,661 --> 01:03:16,793
but you have to promise

918
01:03:16,836 --> 01:03:19,317
not to steal
any more of my pup treats.

919
01:03:20,709 --> 01:03:22,886
Oh, come on!

920
01:03:29,066 --> 01:03:32,069
<i>This is Gene and Heidi.</i>
<i>We're stuck in a mudslide.</i>

921
01:03:32,112 --> 01:03:34,288
<i>We need an evac... ASAP!</i>

922
01:03:34,332 --> 01:03:35,550
Copy that, Gene.

923
01:03:35,594 --> 01:03:37,204
I've got eyes
on your location.

924
01:03:46,039 --> 01:03:47,388
Okay, change of plan.

925
01:03:47,432 --> 01:03:50,348
I can't fly.
There's too much ash in the air.

926
01:03:50,391 --> 01:03:52,916
We're gonna have to do
this rescue from the ground.

927
01:03:59,574 --> 01:04:01,707
Chase, I'm gonna need backup.

928
01:04:01,750 --> 01:04:03,143
<i>Already on my way.</i>

929
01:04:10,716 --> 01:04:12,979
Marshall, this is Ryder.

930
01:04:13,023 --> 01:04:14,763
Any sign of Rhubarb?

931
01:04:14,807 --> 01:04:15,939
<i>Not yet.</i>

932
01:04:15,982 --> 01:04:18,376
But I'm not coming in
until I find him.

933
01:04:24,991 --> 01:04:26,123
There they are!

934
01:04:26,166 --> 01:04:28,212
Over here!
Help!

935
01:04:28,255 --> 01:04:30,431
Hang on!
We're coming!

936
01:04:30,475 --> 01:04:32,433
Skye, I'm gonna fire
my grappling hook

937
01:04:32,477 --> 01:04:33,826
across to you.

938
01:04:33,870 --> 01:04:34,914
Ready when you are.

939
01:04:34,958 --> 01:04:35,872
Fire!

940
01:04:38,483 --> 01:04:39,440
Nice shot.

941
01:04:40,006 --> 01:04:41,138
Bullseye!

942
01:04:42,269 --> 01:04:43,836
Get on!

943
01:04:43,880 --> 01:04:45,882
Got it!
Whoa.

944
01:04:45,925 --> 01:04:47,927
And up we go!

945
01:04:55,587 --> 01:04:57,806
Climb toward me!

946
01:04:58,851 --> 01:05:01,288
Climb, climb,
climb!

947
01:05:01,332 --> 01:05:03,160
Uh-oh. Hill!

948
01:05:04,683 --> 01:05:07,599
Oh-- Whoa!

949
01:05:10,471 --> 01:05:12,996
Okay, let's try that again.

950
01:05:16,825 --> 01:05:20,568
If this rope hits that rock,
it's going to cut it in half!

951
01:05:20,612 --> 01:05:23,702
Okay, I'm climbing,
I'm climbing!

952
01:05:28,489 --> 01:05:30,274
You're
almost there! Grab on!

953
01:05:30,317 --> 01:05:33,930
Oh, No, no, no, no, no!

954
01:05:33,973 --> 01:05:35,540
Whoa!

955
01:05:35,583 --> 01:05:38,021
This is getting ridiculous!

956
01:05:38,064 --> 01:05:39,239
It's now or never.

957
01:05:41,415 --> 01:05:43,461
Time to take the high road.

958
01:05:57,257 --> 01:05:58,476
Got them!

959
01:06:00,478 --> 01:06:01,392
Yeah!

960
01:06:01,435 --> 01:06:03,524
Nice catch, Skye!

961
01:06:03,568 --> 01:06:05,744
Hang on.

962
01:06:13,839 --> 01:06:15,884
Rhubarb! Rhubarb!

963
01:06:18,191 --> 01:06:19,105
Rhubarb!

964
01:06:20,280 --> 01:06:21,281
Rhubarb!

965
01:06:25,590 --> 01:06:27,157
Rhubarb?

966
01:06:27,200 --> 01:06:28,985
Rhubarb, where are you?

967
01:06:29,028 --> 01:06:31,378
Come on, buddy,
we've got to get out of here!

968
01:06:35,295 --> 01:06:36,383
Rhubarb!

969
01:06:38,646 --> 01:06:41,519
Well, look who it is.

970
01:06:41,562 --> 01:06:43,390
Humdinger!

971
01:06:43,434 --> 01:06:44,826
Look what
you've done!

972
01:06:44,870 --> 01:06:48,395
Oh, no.
You're not going to pin this on me.

973
01:06:48,439 --> 01:06:51,181
You and the PAW Patrol
love to blame old Humdinger

974
01:06:51,224 --> 01:06:52,617
for everything!

975
01:06:52,660 --> 01:06:54,706
Where are the rest
of your friends now,

976
01:06:54,749 --> 01:06:57,143
little puppy dog?

977
01:06:57,187 --> 01:06:59,363
It's just you and me.

978
01:07:11,549 --> 01:07:13,725
Yeah, Rhubarb!

979
01:07:22,560 --> 01:07:24,475
Now that's a roar!

980
01:07:29,828 --> 01:07:33,614
Everybody, get under cover!
We'll be safe in the cavern.

981
01:07:39,011 --> 01:07:40,534
Come on, come on!

982
01:07:43,320 --> 01:07:46,975
Is that the last of the dinos?
Is everybody safe?

983
01:07:47,019 --> 01:07:50,153
No. Marshall and Rhubarb
are still out there.

984
01:07:56,724 --> 01:07:58,857
Don't worry.
We'll be out of this soon.

985
01:07:58,900 --> 01:08:00,989
We're gonna take cover
in the cavern.

986
01:08:02,774 --> 01:08:04,471
Let's clear a path!

987
01:08:06,473 --> 01:08:09,563
<i>♪ We're going places</i>
<i>We've never been</i>

988
01:08:09,607 --> 01:08:12,392
<i>♪ Off to the races</i>
<i>We about to win</i>

989
01:08:12,436 --> 01:08:15,700
<i>♪ I feel amazing</i>
<i>Ten out of ten</i>

990
01:08:15,743 --> 01:08:17,136
<i>♪ Let's go</i>

991
01:08:17,180 --> 01:08:18,964
<i>♪ Let's go</i>
Ooh...

992
01:08:19,007 --> 01:08:21,923
<i>♪ Hands up if you're ready</i>

993
01:08:21,967 --> 01:08:24,709
<i>♪ Hold up, keep it steady</i>
Rhubarb, what are you doing?

994
01:08:24,752 --> 01:08:27,712
<i>♪ Go off like confetti</i>

995
01:08:27,755 --> 01:08:30,497
<i>♪ Hold on tight</i>

996
01:08:30,541 --> 01:08:33,674
<i>♪ You better work</i>
<i>Ooh-ooh</i>

997
01:08:33,718 --> 01:08:36,416
<i>♪ You better work</i>
<i>Ooh-ooh</i>

998
01:08:36,460 --> 01:08:39,115
<i>♪ Let's get to work</i>
Yeah, Rhubarb!

999
01:08:39,158 --> 01:08:41,726
Nice moves! You're a natural!

1000
01:08:41,769 --> 01:08:43,902
<i>♪ Work, work, work, work ♪</i>

1001
01:08:57,568 --> 01:08:58,525
Marshall!

1002
01:08:59,135 --> 01:09:00,310
Marshall!

1003
01:09:02,312 --> 01:09:03,356
We're trapped!

1004
01:09:03,400 --> 01:09:05,576
Everybody, stand back!

1005
01:09:17,370 --> 01:09:20,852
It's not working!
There's not enough water!

1006
01:09:28,686 --> 01:09:31,732
If I can get up that cliff
and release that water,

1007
01:09:31,776 --> 01:09:33,560
we might stand a chance.

1008
01:09:36,346 --> 01:09:38,174
Marshall,
what are you doing?

1009
01:09:39,000 --> 01:09:40,176
On my signal,

1010
01:09:40,219 --> 01:09:42,090
point the water cannons
straight down.

1011
01:09:44,136 --> 01:09:45,050
Ready...

1012
01:09:47,226 --> 01:09:48,227
aim...

1013
01:09:50,447 --> 01:09:51,317
fire!

1014
01:10:05,549 --> 01:10:07,638
He's trying to cross it.

1015
01:10:10,075 --> 01:10:11,381
It's working!

1016
01:10:15,776 --> 01:10:17,343
Marshall, hurry!

1017
01:10:17,865 --> 01:10:18,997
Huh?

1018
01:10:25,395 --> 01:10:27,832
No, no!
Come on, come on!

1019
01:10:28,485 --> 01:10:30,182
No, no!

1020
01:10:31,836 --> 01:10:33,141
Marshall!

1021
01:10:33,185 --> 01:10:34,839
Rhubarb, get out of there!

